+/*
+ * SWEET GPU phase 1, Poco F1 (beryllium, SDM845): Adreno 630 power-up.
+ * OFF by default. Boot-arg sweetgpu=N; every stage logs "SWEET GPU:" and
+ * stops at the first failure without touching anything it cannot undo:
+ *
+ *   0  nothing (default)
+ *   1  read-only probe: GCC/GPU CC clock + GDSC state, GMU registers only
+ *      when CX and the GMU clocks are already on
+ *   2  1, then power the CX GDSC and the GMU clocks, dump the GPU SMMU
+ *      (read-only) and test GMU ITCM/DTCM read/write (GMU held in reset)
+ *   3  2, then cold-boot the GMU firmware (a630_gmu.bin) up to 0xBABEFACE
+ *      and hold it in reset again
+ *   4  GMU memory + GPU SMMU context bank, HFI queue table, GMU boot and
+ *      the v1 HFI handshake (INIT, FW_VER, PERF_TBL, BW_VOTE_TBL, TEST)
+ *   5  4 + GX rail (GMU boot OOB at the lowest DCVS level), SPTPRAC, the
+ *      GPU OOB, then read the GX GDSC and first GPU core registers; slumber
+ *   6  5 + signed zap shader (a630_zap) through TrustZone PAS id 13 while
+ *      GX is on: INIT_IMAGE, MEM_SETUP, copy, AUTH_AND_RESET, SHUTDOWN
+ *   7  6 + CP bring-up in the order of Linux a6xx hw_init: CP/UCHE/VBIF
+ *      configuration, SQE (a630_sqe.fw) + ring buffer in a GPU SMMU context
+ *      (stream ID 0), SQE_CNTL=1, CP_ME_INIT, zap, CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0, then
+ *      a NOP/MEM_WRITE/CACHE_FLUSH_TS submission with timestamp readback
+ *
+ * Stages >= 3 need firmware: files under /usr/standalone/firmware/sweet/
+ * of the iOS root (a630_gmu.bin, a630_sqe.fw, a630_zap.mdt + a630_zap.bNN)
+ * or, without a root image yet, ADT properties of /sweet-gpu (gmu-firmware,
+ * sqe-firmware, zap-mdt, zap-b00..zap-b09). The stages run on a kernel
+ * thread that waits (boot-arg sweetgpuwait=seconds, default 600) for them.
+ * See docs/GPU_A630_BRINGUP.md.
+ *
+ * Provenance: the structure and the hardware-proven register sequences are
+ * ported from mxtpasontop/ios-sweet branch gpu (Adreno 618 on the same XNU
+ * code base, patches 0078-0098; no licence file in that repository), with
+ * the SDM845 values from Linux drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_*.c,
+ * drivers/clk/qcom/gpucc-sdm845.c, gcc-sdm845.c (GPL-2.0-only: register
+ * numbers and sequences only, no code copied) and the phone's live DT
